      {
        "id": 210907,
        "name": "Jeysie",
        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-12-15T10:34:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mwc146\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n mwc146:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Well, this is Prime Wardens AA – he sets up at double the speed and can really come out swinging. Argent Adept&nbsp; <em>usually</em>  just supports others, but he has consistent damage in his deck and can buff himself considerably. All he'd really have to do is keep neutralizing Naturalist until he's ready to pull out all the instruments and chain together a dozen instances of damage, each of them buffed.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Especially since it pretty much just stops at \"neutralizing Naturalist\" anyway; when Naturalist is down to being just Michael Conteh, Argent's basically like \"GG, dude\".</p>",
