      {
        "id": 210911,
        "name": "The Almighty Weasel",
        "username": "The_Almighty_Weasel",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_almighty_weasel/{size}/2130_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-12-17T23:34:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Jeysie\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/48/1868_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jeysie:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I was rooting for Blade for just about his every match, really, for the entertainment value. I especially loved the special brand of sheer pettiness in the wholly unnecessary tasering of the Chairman. But yeah, watching Fanatic go down to one of the most normal participants in the whole thing was particularly entertaining.Felt pretty conflicted when he got to facing AZ, though. Poor AZ. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/frowning.png?v=12\" title=\":frowning:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":frowning:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Right there with you on rooting for Blade! It's an issue I have with a lot of Superhero stories. They often come down to a contest of brain versus brawn, where brawn is the hero and brain the villain. I tend to sympathise the other way. But I digress.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Haka losing in any kind of physical contest was insane, considering that C&amp;A told us that writers had to keep coming up with reasons why he couldn't just show up and shut down every major plot event. I mean, sure, Fanatic is cool and all, but very little in her episode indicated that she possessed that level of power.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>KNYFE vs Stuntman was crazy, though the idea of the Rogue Agent suit being less combat-oriented kind of gave that some legs. Once again, nothing in Ancel G Moreau's episode indicated that getting up after being knocked down was a particularly special power of his.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Nightmist beating Mister Fixer was kind of a surprise, but the takeaway from this and the Nightmist episode is that Nightmist has the greatest number of plot devices in her possession.</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:41:20.441Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
