      {
        "id": 210912,
        "name": "Jeysie",
        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-12-18T00:29:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"The Almighty Weasel\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n The Almighty Weasel:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Right there with you on rooting for Blade! It's an issue I have with a lot of Superhero stories. They often come down to a contest of brain versus brawn, where brawn is the hero and brain the villain. I tend to sympathise the other way. But I digress.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, I know one reason why I felt more interested in Marvel over DC over the years was that Marvel seemed to have a much larger quantity of science heroes and science being awesome versus the smart people being villains and science being bad.</p>\n<p>But I'm still willing to appreciate Baron Blade being one of the most mad sciencey mad scientists to ever mad science.</p>",
